// Edge: (count for ...) == 1 — direct aggregate equality with non-zero
// literal, no exists wrapper. Confirms that direct aggregate comparison
// works for non-zero values (== 0 also works — see case 1149).
// Note: count deduplicates by the bound timepoint variable, so two Logins
// with identical field values at different times still count as distinct tp's
// — but here count remains 1 at tp4 because formerly sees only 1 distinct
// matching tp at a time (the aggregate scans within the window per-tp).
// At tp0: 0 Logins, 0==1 false. At tp2: 1 Login, 1==1 true.
// At tp4: still 1==1 true (see above).

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Alert",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    (count for (t: Timepoint). where (formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: context.input.server } && tp(t))) == 1
};
